<title>JAPAN: Mitsui Eng, Brown &amp; Root to build chemical plants.</title>
<headline>Mitsui Eng, Brown &amp; Root to build chemical plants.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsui Engineering &amp; Shipbuilding Co Ltd said on Tuesday that it had agreed with Brown &amp; Root Inc of the United States to jointly build petroleum and chemical plants in the Asia-Pacific.</p>
<p>Mitsui and an arm of Brown &amp; Root will jointly seek plant construction orders in the region, Mitsui said in a statement.</p>
<p>In April, the two companies agreed to cooperate in the production of ethylene and other orefinic hydrocarbon materials. Ethylene is used to make such products as film and plastic bottles.</p>
<p>Brown &amp; Root is part of the Halliburton Co group.</p>
</text>
